WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.401
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.702
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:05.371
You're here, you made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:09.375 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.111
This morning,
the world's richest man,

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:15.547 line:0%
Elon Musk, was named "Time"
magazine's Person of the Year.

00:00:15.547 --> 00:00:16.950 line:0%
Yeah.
Musk received the honor

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.918 line:0%
for his work
in space exploration

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.120
and after he bought
10 million subscriptions

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.790
to "Time" magazine.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.292
I'm kidding.
Although it was a little strange

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.027
that everyone at "Time"
drove into work today

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:30.830
in a brand-new Tesla.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.799
Being named Person of the Year
is a big deal.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.533
It's basically
Sexiest Man Alive,

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.870
but you're competing against
the Dalai Lama and the Pope.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.037
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.238
It was actually
a pretty competitive year.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.707
The other finalists
were the scientists

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.342
behind the COVID vaccine
and the lawyer who appeared

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.044
at a Zoom trial
with a cat filter.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.279
-Can you hear me, Judge?

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.648
I'm here live.
I'm not -- I'm not a cat.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.317
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.653
-Some news from Washington.
Today, President Biden signed

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.355
an executive order aimed at
improving customer experience

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.891 line:0%
for government services,
like renewing passports

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:01.060 line:0%
and filing taxes.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.196
Yeah, now when you get audited,
the IRS agent

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.898
draws a little smiley face
on your return.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.966
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.468
And this is nice.
Now, when you're on hold

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.102
for two hours,
instead of light jazz,

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:13.706
they play even lighter jazz.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.809
Hey, I saw that former
Vice President Mike Pence

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.744
has been touring key election
states, like New Hampshire.

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:20.312
A lot of people think
that he could be gearing up

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.882
for a presidential run in 2024.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.817
He's even been testing out
some campaign slogans

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.319
to see what people respond to.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.289
Check some of these out.
First up, there's "Pence 2024 --

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.391
I make Mitt Romney
look like Post Malone."

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.726
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:37.230
Next, there's "Pence 2024 --
I call ketchup hot sauce."

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.132
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.069
And, finally,
there's "Pence 2024 --

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:45.772
One time, I heard
a Megan Thee Stallion song

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.873
and fainted."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:50.543
I think that's the one.
-Wow, yeah! That's the one.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:54.346
-"Mother!"
-"Mother!"

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:56.515
-Oh, I heard that,
in a new documentary,

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:59.485
Russian President Vladimir Putin
revealed that, back in the '90s,

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:03.056 line:0%
he worked as a cab driver
to make ends meet.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.957
Yep, it was the only cab
where you got in

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.492
and the driver told you
where you're going.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.194
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.730
"We're taking detour."
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.332
It was the last time Putin
drove a car

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.333
where the "passenger"
wasn't in the trunk.

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.669
[ Laughter, scattered groans ]

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.004
Hey, this is cool --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.004 --> 00:02:21.507
-Wow!
-Listen to this.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.643
New FDA-approved eye drops
just hit the market

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:27.780 line:0%
that provide better vision
for up to 10 hours.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.481 line:0%
And they could replace
reading glasses

00:02:29.481 --> 00:02:31.183 line:0%
for millions of Americans.

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:33.019
Yeah, which means your dad
will now walk around

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.288
looking for the eye drops that
are on the top of his head.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:38.457
[ Laughter ]
"Where did I put --"

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:39.726
You know some guy's
gonna be like,

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.794
"I bet if I use the whole
bottle, I could see Mars."

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.397
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.132
Now when you notice someone
putting in eye drops,

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.234
you can play the fun new game,
"Reader or Stoner?"

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.636
It's cool. It's fun.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:52.404
Well, get this --
authorities in New Zealand

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:54.473 line:0%
are investigating after one man
apparently got

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:58.911 line:0%
10 COVID vaccine shots
on the same day

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:01.848
and pretended to be
a different person each time.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.348
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.348 --> 00:03:05.884
If you asked what he got,
he says, "Johnson and Johnson

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:07.587
and Johnson and Johnson
and Johnson and Johnson."

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.389
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.290
It was weird at his office
holiday party when he was like,

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.393
"So, how did you guys
feel after the ninth dose?

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:16.361
That one kind of got me."

00:03:16.361 --> 00:03:18.330
You guys hear about this?
A Michigan woman is currently

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.499
facing up to nine years
in prison

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:24.137 line:0%
after she went to a fake website
called "Rent-A-Hitman"

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:28.141 line:0%
and offered $5,000 to have
her ex-husband killed.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.375
Yeah, you could tell
she was nervous.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.045
Today, she logged into
Bribe-A-Judge.org.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.079
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:35.748
Well, guys, this is big.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.283
Last night the January 6th
commission revealed that

00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:41.087 line:0%
during the Capitol riots,
the White House Chief of Staff

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:44.157 line:0%
got texts pleading for Trump
to calm things down

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:47.493 line:0%
from Fox News anchors
and Donald Trump Jr.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.995
[ Audience murmurs ]
Yeah.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.731
Trump ignored the advice
of the closest to him

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.566
and also Don Jr.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.303
Trump was like, "If I replied
to every text that said

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.472
'What you're doing is crazy,'
I'd never get anything done."

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.207
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.741
Yeah, it came out
that Fox News hosts

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:04.276
were begging Trump
to do something.

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.979
And today, Fox News hosts
lit their tree on fire again

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:09.549
just to change the subject.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.184
[ Applause ]

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:13.753
Trump didn't want to hear it.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.822
Not only did he ignore the texts
from Fox News,

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.357
he also dropped them from
his family cellphone plan.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:19.959
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.428
That's right, White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows was

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.397
getting texts during the attack
asking Trump to intervene.

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:28.334
For example, Sean Hannity
texted -- and this is real --

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.770
"Can he make a statement, ask
people to leave the Capitol?"

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.840
Yep, that's not all Meadows
received.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.407
Several other messages that day
too.

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:37.109
For example, Eric Trump texted,

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.178
"Head stuck in Capitol
staircase railing.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.780
Send help!"

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.382
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.317
Next up, Rudy Giuliani texted,

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.753
"Just showed up
at Capitol Total Landscaping.

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:49.388
When's the riotin' start?"

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:51.090
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.325
And finally President Trump
texted Meadows,

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:55.228
"Just make sure they don't take
away my Twitter!"

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.429
Yeah, there you go.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:59.432
Crazy day all around.
Crazy day all around.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:02.367
[ Applause ]

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.936
Some more news from Washington.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.771 line:0%
The White House just announced
their plan to add

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:08.141 line:0%
500,000 charging stations

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.309 line:0%
for electric vehicles
across the country.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:11.877
It's incredible.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:14.180
Somehow we can build half
a million charging stations,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.549
but we can't add a second outlet
at LaGuardia.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.150
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:21.086
Can I charge my phone?
I just -- Okay.

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:22.521
You guys hear this?

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:25.224
Today, the state of New York
ordered former governor

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:28.861 line:0%
Andrew Cuomo to return
the $5 million he received from

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.463 line:0%
his book on leadership
during the pandemic.

00:05:31.463 --> 00:05:33.566
I think it's safe
to say the drinking

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.768
at the Cuomo family Christmas
has already begun.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.537
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:40.073
Some business news -- After
announcing their name change,

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:42.407
Facebook paid a bank
in South Dakota

00:05:42.407 --> 00:05:47.046
$60 million for the rights
to their new name, Meta.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:50.315
It's making me emotional because
seeing a bank get $60 million

00:05:50.315 --> 00:05:51.784
is what Christmas is all about.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.920
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.756
[ Applause ]

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.061
That's right, a bank.

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.729
Now they're so rich,
they don't even chain

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.631
their pens to the table anymore.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.733
"Just take them!
That's a Montblanc.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.102
Just take it."

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:12.104
I like how Facebook
was trying to rename

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.239
their company something "cool,"
but it was already being used

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:15.908
by a bank in South Dakota.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.342
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.342 --> 00:06:18.877
Well, this is encouraging.

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:21.147
I read that despite
supply chain issues,

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:24.750 line:0%
UPS and the Postal Service
have improved their on-time

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.486 line:0%
deliveries compared to
last year's holiday season.

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:28.620
That's right.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.123
They now deliver
that little slip that says,

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.224
"Sorry we missed you"
right on time.

00:06:32.224 --> 00:06:34.527
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:38.397
Right on time.
"Ah, I was here all day."

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:42.802 line:0%
I saw that LG has a new
battery-powered TV that you can

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.470 line:0%
wheel around on a stand
to watch anywhere.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.673
Yeah, a TV on wheels.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:49.474
It is perfect
if you've ever dreamt of being

00:06:49.474 --> 00:06:52.144
a substitute teacher from 1997.

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:55.414
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:58.618 line:0%
And get this -- Uber Eats just
made its first-ever delivery

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:02.522 line:0%
to space after a Japanese
billionaire brought food

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:06.225 line:0%
from the app to astronauts on
the International Space Station.

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.893
That's how tough the economy is
right now --

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:09.862
a billionaire is working
for Uber Eats.

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:11.397
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:13.399 line:0%
Well, this is interesting.
A new study found that

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.368 line:0%
rocket scientists
and brain surgeons

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:17.904 line:0%
are not any smarter
than the general population.

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.505 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:21.307
That's got to be a great study
to read right before

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:22.775
you're wheeled in
for brain surgery, right?

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:24.510
It's like, "Huh?"

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:27.079
Brain surgeons were like, "You
need to be super smart to know

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:29.749
about the brain and all those
little tubey things around it."

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.317
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:33.752
And finally, a woman eating at
a restaurant in New Orleans

00:07:33.752 --> 00:07:36.588 line:0%
found a dozen pearls in
an oyster that she ordered.

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:37.890 line:0%
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.058
The woman said she would
probably sell the pearls

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:42.194
when they passed
in six to eight hours.

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:47.166 line:0%
Today, Chinese President
Xi Jinping met virtually

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:50.669 line:0%
with Russian President
Vladimir Putin.

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:52.138
They didn't talk, even.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:55.040
They just spent an hour
exchanging maniacal laughter.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.911
[ Laughing evilly ]

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:01.546
It's not great news for Biden.
I mean, for Marvel fans,

00:08:01.546 --> 00:08:03.415
it's like if Spider-Man
found out that Doc Ock

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:04.883
was Zooming
with the Green Goblin.

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:07.252
I mean, something is happening.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.252 --> 00:08:10.022
But they had a lot to discuss,
like trade, nuclear arms,

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:12.491
and why Carrie
didn't call 9-1-1.

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:13.725
[ Laughter ]

00:08:13.725 --> 00:08:16.595
At one point,
Xi called Putin his old friend,

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:20.032
and Putin called Xi
his dear friend.

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:22.301
Then they ended the call like,
"You hack us first,"

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:25.404
"No, you hack us first!"
"Oh, no, you hack us first!"

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:27.272
[ Laughter ]

00:08:27.272 --> 00:08:29.708
Some big news in Washington.
The House voted to hold

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:32.211 line:0%
former Trump chief of staff
Mark Meadows

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:35.514 line:0%
in criminal contempt of Congress
for refusing to cooperate

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:37.650 line:0%
with the January 6th panel.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.652
The consequences are severe.
Meadows could be sentenced

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.453
to a year in prison,
or, even worse,

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:44.890
another month working for Trump.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.458
Of course,
Meadows needs a good lawyer,

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:47.793
so the first thing he did
was pull up

00:08:47.793 --> 00:08:49.895
Rudy Giuliani's number
and delete it.

00:08:49.895 --> 00:08:51.997
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:54.100
Some more news.
The White House just announced

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.467
that, due to COVID concerns,

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.570
instead of the traditional
holiday parties,

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.273
it's inviting guests
to come see the decorations

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:02.808
on a 30-minute self-guided tour.

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.977
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.945
Which is just a fancy way
of Biden saying,

00:09:06.945 --> 00:09:08.581
"Come if you want,
but I ain't gonna be there."

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:10.115
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:12.484
"I ain't getting COVID."
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:15.087
So guests can now go
on a 30-minute self-guided tour

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:16.589
of an old mansion.

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:17.723
There's actually a name
for that --

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:20.493
it's called a haunted house.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:21.827
That's right.
A self-guided tour

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:23.495
of a historic
Washington building.

00:09:23.495 --> 00:09:26.565
That's basically how Fox News
described January 6th.

00:09:26.565 --> 00:09:29.368
[ Laughter ]

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:34.005 line:0%
Listen to this -- I heard that
pharmacists across the country

00:09:34.005 --> 00:09:36.609 line:0%
are feeling burned out
due to increased demand

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:40.145 line:0%
for COVID shots
and being short-staffed.

00:09:40.145 --> 00:09:42.114
Yeah, I'm sure it's that
and not just hearing

00:09:42.114 --> 00:09:44.183
The Chipmunks Christmas on loop
for two months.

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:47.219
It's like, "I'm losing it, Gary.
I'm losing it.

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:49.021
Get him a hula hoop!
Get him a hula hoop!"

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:51.123
[ Laughter ]

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:52.625
You know your pharmacist
is stressed out

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:53.793
when they disinfect your arm

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:56.128
with the Bacardi
from their flask.

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.330
"Shot for you, shot for me,
right?"

00:09:58.330 --> 00:09:59.898
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.898 --> 00:10:01.867
It's gotten so bad now,
when you order Xanax,

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:04.070
the pharmacist says,
"We just ran out."

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:06.905
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.905 --> 00:10:09.341
Get this.
In Canada, a 5-year-old is safe

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:11.810
after he was caught driving
his parents' car

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.246
to go buy a Christmas present
for his sister.

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:15.847
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:10:15.847 --> 00:10:18.050
The cop asked him to recite
the alphabet backwards,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.286
and he was like, "I haven't even
learned it forwards."

00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:22.454
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.454 --> 00:10:24.223
Yeah, he's in a lot of trouble,

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:26.525
so, really, his sister got
the greatest gift of all.

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:28.360
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.595
Meanwhile, the kid showed
each officer a packet

00:10:30.595 --> 00:10:31.730
of Dunkaroos and said,

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.666
"How about we, uh,
say this never happened?"

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.134
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.134 --> 00:10:36.868
And, finally, this is something
you don't hear every day.

00:10:36.868 --> 00:10:38.904
Authorities in Ohio
are investigating

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:42.141 line:0%
after someone stole
a 58-foot bridge.

00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:43.342 line:0%
[ Light laughter ]

00:10:43.342 --> 00:10:44.977
Police say they're
on the lookout for a thief

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:46.679
who's described
as having dark hair,

00:10:46.679 --> 00:10:48.547
blue eyes, and is the Hulk.

00:10:49.648 --> 00:10:51.650
Well, guys, one of the biggest
movies of the year,

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.287 line:0%
"Spider-Man: No Way Home"
has finally hit theaters.

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:57.556
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:57.556 --> 00:11:00.192
Finally.
Fans are going nuts.

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:02.227
People haven't been this pumped
for a Marvel movie

00:11:02.227 --> 00:11:04.230
since the last one
came out a week ago.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.931
[ Laughter ]

00:11:05.931 --> 00:11:07.933
Yep, everyone's excited
to see it in theaters.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:09.935
Even Dr. Fauci was like,
"Screw it.

00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:11.703
I got to support this guy."
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.703 --> 00:11:13.873
"He's wearing a mask.
Let's go. I'm ready to go."

00:11:13.873 --> 00:11:14.907
[ Laughter ]

00:11:14.907 --> 00:11:16.541
Yep, as we speak,
fans are lined up

00:11:16.541 --> 00:11:18.243
to see the movie,
including plenty of guys

00:11:18.243 --> 00:11:20.712
dressed like Spider-Man
who definitely can't pull off

00:11:20.712 --> 00:11:22.581
dressing like Spider-Man.
You know what I'm saying?

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:25.651
[ Laughter ]

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:27.453
In this movie,
Spider-Man has to fight off

00:11:27.453 --> 00:11:29.254
a bunch of crazy villains
at once.

00:11:29.254 --> 00:11:30.856
And after he does,
he's immediately hired

00:11:30.856 --> 00:11:32.625
as a flight attendant
for United.

00:11:32.625 --> 00:11:34.894
[ Laughter ]

00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:37.229
Speaking of airlines,
in a Senate hearing,

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:39.664 line:0%
the CEOs of Southwest
and American Airlines

00:11:39.664 --> 00:11:43.369 line:0%
both questioned the need
for masks on planes.

00:11:43.369 --> 00:11:45.404
Yep, the same thing
actually happened last month

00:11:45.404 --> 00:11:47.806
with the CEO of Spirit
and pants.

00:11:47.806 --> 00:11:49.641
[ Laughter ]

00:11:49.641 --> 00:11:52.077
Yeah, the Southwest CEO was
like, "Who needs masks?

00:11:52.077 --> 00:11:55.181
There's plenty of fresh air.
We fly with the top down."

00:11:55.181 --> 00:11:57.783
"Buckle up, everybody!"
[ Laughter ]

00:11:57.783 --> 00:11:59.751
Speaking of wearing masks
on planes, I heard about

00:11:59.751 --> 00:12:02.087
one passenger who tried
to work around the rule.

00:12:02.087 --> 00:12:03.355
Listen to this.

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:06.692
-A man is now banned from flying
with United Airlines

00:12:06.692 --> 00:12:10.428
after deciding to mask up
with a bright red thong.

00:12:10.428 --> 00:12:12.231
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:14.934 --> 00:12:17.335
-If you fly Spirit,
that's the oxygen mask

00:12:17.335 --> 00:12:19.204
that drops down in an emergency.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.204 --> 00:12:21.540
Make sure to put it
on yourself first, then...

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:22.674
[ Laughter ]

00:12:22.674 --> 00:12:26.245
-"Dumps like a truck."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:26.245 --> 00:12:28.247
-A few minutes later,
an air marshal walked over

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:29.581
and gave him a mouth wedgie.

00:12:29.581 --> 00:12:31.850
It was interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.485
You guys see this?
Former President Trump

00:12:33.485 --> 00:12:36.255 line:0%
is really upset with his old
chief of staff Mark Meadows

00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:38.223 line:0%
for writing in his book
that Trump's hair

00:12:38.223 --> 00:12:42.294 line:0%
looked awful when he had COVID.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:44.229
Must have looked really bad,
because that's how most people

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:45.898
describe Trump's hair
when he's healthy.

00:12:45.898 --> 00:12:47.299
[ Laughter ]

00:12:47.299 --> 00:12:48.867
Meanwhile, I read
that this holiday season,

00:12:48.867 --> 00:12:51.736 line:0%
Melania Trump is releasing
her first NFT,

00:12:51.736 --> 00:12:53.972 line:0%
called "Melania's Vision,"

00:12:53.972 --> 00:12:56.141 line:0%
which is a watercolor
of her eyes.

00:12:56.141 --> 00:12:58.110
[ Laughter ]

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.444
Donald's like,
"I'm so proud of you.

00:12:59.444 --> 00:13:00.946
Congrats on the 'nuft.'"

00:13:00.946 --> 00:13:03.015
[ Laughter ]

00:13:03.015 --> 00:13:04.283
Yep, Trump's excited about it.

00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:06.818
He thinks NFT stands
for "not filing taxes."

00:13:06.818 --> 00:13:10.022
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:13.725 --> 00:13:15.627
The cool thing
about Melania's NFT,

00:13:15.627 --> 00:13:17.129
just like she does
with her husband,

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:18.964
as soon as you turn away,
the eyes roll.

00:13:18.964 --> 00:13:20.732
[ Laughter ]
It's amazing.

00:13:20.732 --> 00:13:22.167
Hey, this is cool.
In a recent interview,

00:13:22.167 --> 00:13:24.569 line:0%
Usain Bolt said
that playing "Mario Kart"

00:13:24.569 --> 00:13:26.871 line:0%
helped him become
an Olympic champion.

00:13:26.871 --> 00:13:28.573
[ Cheers ]
I'm in shock.

00:13:28.573 --> 00:13:30.242
'Cause apparently I've been
training for the Olympics

00:13:30.242 --> 00:13:33.578
for the last 35 years.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:33.578 --> 00:13:36.582 line:0%
Well, get this.
Here in New York, an MTA manager

00:13:36.582 --> 00:13:40.018 line:0%
was caught with the blow-up doll
in the front seat of his car,

00:13:40.018 --> 00:13:42.621 line:0%
and he's insisting that
he uses it for the company

00:13:42.621 --> 00:13:45.057 line:0%
and not so that he can drive
in the carpool lane.

00:13:45.057 --> 00:13:46.524
[ Laughter ]

00:13:46.524 --> 00:13:48.460
In a related story, he's lying.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.762
[ Laughter ]

00:13:49.762 --> 00:13:51.530
Guy was like, "Look,
if you have a problem with this,

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.632
talk to my lawyer," and then,
he blew up another doll.

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:55.300
[ Laughter ]

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:58.370
And, finally, guys, "Sing 2"
is coming out next week.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.938
I mean,
we are excited about this.

00:13:59.938 --> 00:14:01.473
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.141
It has such an amazing cast,

00:14:03.141 --> 00:14:04.877
and we wanted to do something
fun with the actors.

00:14:04.877 --> 00:14:07.012
So we gave them a bunch
of weird phrases

00:14:07.012 --> 00:14:09.981
and asked them to sneak those
phrases into their interviews

00:14:09.981 --> 00:14:11.783
as casually as possible.

00:14:11.783 --> 00:14:13.719
No one knew we were doing this.
So check it out.

00:14:13.719 --> 00:14:16.088
It's time for "Drop It In."

00:14:16.088 --> 00:14:18.090
-♪ Drop It In, Drop It In ♪

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:20.859
♪ D-D-D-D-Drop It In, yeah ♪

00:14:20.859 --> 00:14:24.329 line:0%
-Obviously, everyone's going
to watch "Sing 2" for Christmas.

00:14:24.329 --> 00:14:25.497 line:0%
How do you guys plan on

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:27.265 line:0%
celebrating Christmas
this year?

00:14:27.265 --> 00:14:30.536 line:0%
-I'm just going to eat
a lot of food, I feel like,

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:32.837 line:0%
'cause, you know,
you know what they say --

00:14:32.837 --> 00:14:35.374 line:0%
if you can't lick the spoon,
just eat the bowl, you know?

00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:36.608 line:0%
-That's right.

00:14:36.608 --> 00:14:39.277 line:0%
-Which of the following
is not a marsupial --

00:14:39.277 --> 00:14:43.081 line:0%
kangaroo, koala, or platypus?

00:14:43.081 --> 00:14:45.884 line:0%
-Koala.
-Platypus have no pouches.

00:14:45.884 --> 00:14:48.587 line:0%
They're the only
egg-laying mammal.

00:14:48.587 --> 00:14:53.625 line:0%
-Pouches, eggs,
grape nuts, go nuts.

00:14:53.625 --> 00:14:55.594 line:0%
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:55.594 --> 00:14:56.594 line:0%
Yeah.

00:14:56.594 --> 00:14:58.964 line:0%
-I think it's also a movie
about --

00:14:58.964 --> 00:15:03.802 line:0%
about overcoming your own
personal obstacles and --

00:15:03.802 --> 00:15:07.072 line:0%
I mean, even the Pringles Guy
gets lonely in January.

00:15:07.072 --> 00:15:08.740 line:0%
-How many "Sing" stories
do you want to tell?

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.742 line:0%
Like, have you thought
of what you would write

00:15:10.742 --> 00:15:12.911 line:0%
for "Sing 3" or "Sing 4"?
-There could be a "Sing 3,"

00:15:12.911 --> 00:15:17.382 line:0%
"Sing 4," "Sing 5," "Sing 6,"
"Sing 7," "Sing 8" --

00:15:17.382 --> 00:15:19.918 line:0%
"Sing 8," yeah -- "Sing 9,"
"Sing 10," "Sing 11,"

00:15:19.918 --> 00:15:21.553 line:0%
-It'd be like the KIDZ BOP
version of movies!

00:15:21.553 --> 00:15:24.456 line:0%
-..."Sing 12." Yeah! I mean,
you'd skip 13 because of,

00:15:24.456 --> 00:15:26.592 line:0%
you know, bad vibes.
-Yeah, no, you can never...

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:27.960 line:0%
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.028 line:0%
-But, no, I think, otherwise,
it could go on forever.

00:15:30.028 --> 00:15:33.665 line:0%
-So, this was obviously,
like, filming during the pand--

00:15:33.665 --> 00:15:35.600 line:0%
Did you guys get to get together
at any point?

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:39.304 line:0%
-Oh!
They're g-r-r-rape!

00:15:39.304 --> 00:15:41.406 line:0%
As T the Tiger says.

00:15:41.406 --> 00:15:42.607 line:0%
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:42.607 --> 00:15:43.942 line:0%
They're g-r-rape!

00:15:43.942 --> 00:15:45.677 line:0%
-That's sort of the fun
of show business.

00:15:45.677 --> 00:15:47.145 line:0%
And the hard part is, you know,

00:15:47.145 --> 00:15:50.282 line:0%
you get ready, and then there's
someone who can tell you no,

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:53.452 line:0%
and it's deflating, you know?

00:15:53.452 --> 00:15:55.921 line:0%
It's never a great idea
to microwave a balloon.

00:15:55.921 --> 00:15:57.523 line:0%
[ Ding ]
...and I think that the beauty

00:15:57.523 --> 00:15:59.858 line:0%
of this cast of characters is,
they don't stop.

00:15:59.858 --> 00:16:02.761 line:0%
-In the film, Buster Moon has
to tell a little white lie.

00:16:02.761 --> 00:16:05.463 line:0%
I'm curious to know
if you've ever had to exaggerate

00:16:05.463 --> 00:16:08.099 line:0%
a special skill to either land
a role or get ahead.

00:16:08.099 --> 00:16:11.336 line:0%
-I never will tell a white lie.

00:16:11.336 --> 00:16:15.207 line:0%
And that's something I learned
when I once

00:16:15.207 --> 00:16:17.409 line:0%
put a balloon
inside of a microwave,

00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:19.744 line:0%
and it's never a good idea to
put a balloon in a microwave.

00:16:19.744 --> 00:16:21.513 line:0%
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:21.513 --> 00:16:23.682 line:0%
I just have
one last thing to say.

00:16:23.682 --> 00:16:27.252 line:0%
Nunca es un buen idea poner
un globo en el microondo.

00:16:27.252 --> 00:16:28.687 line:0%
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:28.687 --> 00:16:32.056 line:0%
And that's something that is
really important to remember.

00:16:32.056 --> 00:16:34.226 line:0%
-[ Laughs ] Thank you
for sharing that tip with us.

00:16:34.226 --> 00:16:36.561
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:36.561 --> 00:16:38.897
-We are one week away
from Christmas.

00:16:38.897 --> 00:16:40.532
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:43.234 --> 00:16:47.038
Just seven more days,
just eight more sleeps,

00:16:47.038 --> 00:16:48.873
and 900 more Hallmark movies.

00:16:48.873 --> 00:16:51.210
That's it.
We're almost there.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:53.411
That's right, we're one week
away from Christmas.

00:16:53.411 --> 00:16:55.414
Or as the Panera gift cards
at Walgreens call it,

00:16:55.414 --> 00:16:58.650
"Our time to shine."
[ Laughter ]

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:00.952
That's right, Christmas is just
seven days away,

00:17:00.952 --> 00:17:03.355
which means that you'll finish
your chocolate advent calendar

00:17:03.355 --> 00:17:05.424
in...10 days ago.

00:17:05.424 --> 00:17:06.925
[ Laughter ]

00:17:06.925 --> 00:17:08.460
At this point, everyone's
advent calendar

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.295
is starting to look like
an abandoned Motel 6.

00:17:10.295 --> 00:17:12.798
It's sort of sad.
[ Laughter ]

00:17:12.798 --> 00:17:15.133
But you can tell the whole city
is in the holiday spirit.

00:17:15.133 --> 00:17:16.968
I mean, right now,
Times Square Elmo

00:17:16.968 --> 00:17:18.637
reeks of eggnog
instead of vodka.

00:17:18.637 --> 00:17:20.071
And that just...

00:17:20.071 --> 00:17:21.373
Get this, guys.

00:17:21.373 --> 00:17:23.541
According to a new poll,
this year a majority of people

00:17:23.541 --> 00:17:25.877
started their Christmas shopping
before November.

00:17:25.877 --> 00:17:27.045
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:17:27.045 --> 00:17:28.847
Mostly because nobody's known
what month it is

00:17:28.847 --> 00:17:31.650
since March 2020.
[ Laughter ]

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.819
I saw in a recent survey that
most Americans would rather

00:17:33.819 --> 00:17:36.521
get an experience than a gift.

00:17:36.521 --> 00:17:38.556
Well, their partner's gonna be
like, "Well, now you can enjoy

00:17:38.556 --> 00:17:41.193
the experience of owning socks.
There you go."

00:17:41.193 --> 00:17:42.594
[ Laughter ]

00:17:42.594 --> 00:17:44.095
This is amazing --
Experts predict that

00:17:44.095 --> 00:17:47.399
by the end of January,
$120 billion worth of gifts

00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:49.568
will be returned.

00:17:49.568 --> 00:17:51.636
Yep, on Christmas morning,
we exchange presents,

00:17:51.636 --> 00:17:54.306
and on Christmas afternoon,
we exchange receipts.

00:17:54.306 --> 00:17:56.141
[ Laughter ]

00:17:56.141 --> 00:17:58.343
I read that this year's top
toy gifts include

00:17:58.343 --> 00:18:01.180
the Magic Mixies
Magical Misting Cauldron

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:04.015
and WowWee's Got2Glow
Fairy Finder.

00:18:04.015 --> 00:18:06.117
-Ooh, nice.
Did you get either one of those?

00:18:06.117 --> 00:18:08.119
-No, I ended up not going for

00:18:08.119 --> 00:18:09.954
a Magic Mixies
Magical Misting Cauldron

00:18:09.954 --> 00:18:11.957
or WowWee's Got2Glow
Fairy Finder.

00:18:11.957 --> 00:18:13.959
But I did consider getting
the World of Wacky Wonder

00:18:13.959 --> 00:18:15.293
Wizard Worms.

00:18:15.293 --> 00:18:17.129
-Not the Nerdy Naughty Gnomes?

00:18:17.129 --> 00:18:18.496
-Well, I was tempted by

00:18:18.496 --> 00:18:20.833
the Enchanting Earl's
Underwater Otter Oasis,

00:18:20.833 --> 00:18:23.001
but I'd be lying if I said
I didn't think about picking up

00:18:23.001 --> 00:18:26.004
some Charming Chucky Enchanted
Choo-Choo Train Chomping Chimps.

00:18:26.004 --> 00:18:28.173
-Ooh. I love those.

00:18:28.173 --> 00:18:31.343
Are those made by the same
people who made the toad one?

00:18:31.343 --> 00:18:33.344
-Talking about
Twiggy the Trendy Twitter Toad

00:18:33.344 --> 00:18:35.714
or Tommy the Ticklish
Texas Toad?

00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:36.881
-Either one.

00:18:36.881 --> 00:18:38.383
-They're both sold out.
-Oh.

00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:40.919
-They only had Talented Tacky's
Tasteful Tap-dancing Tank-diving

00:18:40.919 --> 00:18:42.320
Turtle Taxis.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:44.856
And Fabulously Fancy Foamy
Fluffy the Fantastic Fighting

00:18:44.856 --> 00:18:47.525
French Falcon.
-Those are good options,

00:18:47.525 --> 00:18:49.261
but I also hear the best toy
of the year is the --

00:18:49.261 --> 00:18:51.196
-Bawitdaba Da Bang Da Dang
Diggy Diggy Shake Up the Boogie

00:18:51.196 --> 00:18:53.065
Said Up Jump the Boogie Dogs?
[ Laughter ]

00:18:53.065 --> 00:18:54.666
-Exactly.

00:18:54.666 --> 00:18:57.401
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:18:57.401 --> 00:18:59.404
-Yeah, I heard that, too.

00:18:59.404 --> 00:19:02.241
[ Chuckles ] Anyway, what are
you getting your kids this year?

00:19:02.241 --> 00:19:04.076
-Uhhh, gift card to Dunkin'.

00:19:04.076 --> 00:19:05.243
[ Laughter ]

00:19:05.243 --> 00:19:06.812
-Me too!
-Oh, my God!

00:19:11.149 --> 00:19:13.151
[ Applause ]

00:19:13.151 --> 00:19:15.821
-Moving on.

00:19:15.821 --> 00:19:17.656
This is very funny.
A woman in California

00:19:17.656 --> 00:19:20.658
got into the holiday spirit
by turning her cubicle at work

00:19:20.658 --> 00:19:22.226
into a gingerbread house.

00:19:22.226 --> 00:19:24.228
This is real.
Check this out.

00:19:24.228 --> 00:19:25.731
-Aw.
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:19:25.731 --> 00:19:27.232
-It looks like one of those huts

00:19:27.232 --> 00:19:29.568
where mall Santas go to vape
on their break.

00:19:29.568 --> 00:19:32.237
[ Laughter ]

00:19:32.237 --> 00:19:35.240
When they show around
new employees, they're like,

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.241
"And that's Carol.

00:19:37.241 --> 00:19:38.910
She's...a lot."

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:40.746
[ Laughter ]

00:19:44.249 --> 00:19:46.752
"She's...mm...

00:19:46.752 --> 00:19:48.420
Yep."

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:49.821
Finally, I heard that this month

00:19:49.821 --> 00:19:51.990
Mariah Carey's "All I Want
for Christmas Is You" became

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:55.160 line:0%
the first holiday song
to hit 1 billion streams

